{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"`docs/adr/0004:43-48` asserts the snapshot-entry shape \"has a single source of truth... Both the\nfetcher's output and the differs' expectations target it. When a new field is added to the\nsnapshot, update the schema first.\" Nothing enforces that.\n\n`_engine/rebar_reconciler/_snapshot_schema.py` (228 LOC) is imported by NO production module; the\nintended producer `fetcher.py` never imports it. The originating story declared\n`fetcher.py (producer validates vs schema)` as file impact; that wiring never landed.\n\nThe schema encodes a `parent` present-vs-absent distinction that gates an inbound CLEAR — a\ndata-destroying path whose own history contains a revert titled \"Revert the inbound parent clear:\nit destroys data.\"\n\nRefined during approval: rather than a bespoke contract test, move the contract into\n`src/rebar/schemas/` where ~90 sibling schemas already live, loaded via `schemas.load()` and\nvalidated with `jsonschema` on a `Draft202012Validator`, with a generated TypedDict layer under a\nCI drift gate (`python -m rebar.schemas.gen_types`, `_build-and-test.yml:545`). The snapshot\ncontract is the odd one out — a hand-rolled Python module outside that machinery, which is *why*\nnothing enforces it while 90 siblings are enforced automatically.\n\nReal fetcher output exists for fixtures: `bridge_state/snapshots/` holds 548 files spanning\n2026-06-11..06-29 with fully-populated entries. It is gitignored and contains PII\n(`emailAddress`, `displayName`, `accountId`), so a small redacted fixture must be derived into the\ntracked `tests/fixtures/jira/`, covering all three observed shapes: populated, `parent`-absent,\nand horizon-trimmed-empty.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The snapshot-entry contract lives in `src/rebar/schemas/` and is loadable via `schemas.load()`\n- [x] It is covered by the existing generated-types drift gate rather than a one-off check\n- [x] A redacted fixture in `tests/fixtures/jira/` covers populated, `parent`-absent, and empty shapes\n- [x] A fetcher field change that diverges from the contract fails CI\n- [x] ADR 0004 describes the enforcement that actually exists"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786086572199285001,"uuid":"5abbf6c5-d398-4a45-b09d-44e8cabffe60"}